{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בארון", :translit "ba'aron", :gloss "concerning the ark"} {:he "ובמזבח הנחשת", :translit "uvemizbeach ha-nechoshet", :gloss "and the bronze altar"} {:he "כתיב בדיו", :translit "katuv badav", :gloss "it is written 'its staves'"} {:he "ובשלחן", :translit "uvashulchan", :gloss "and concerning the table"} {:he "ובמזבח הזהב", :translit "uvemizbeach hazahav", :gloss "and the golden altar"} {:he "כתיב לבתים לבדים", :translit "katuv labatim labadim", :gloss "it is written 'for the houses, for the staves'"} {:he "ב את בדיו", :translit "ba'et badav", :gloss "in 'its staves'"} {:he "לרבות הבתים", :translit "lerabot ha-batim", :gloss "to include the houses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic comparison: בדיו used for ark and bronze altar; לבתים לבדים for table and golden altar"} {:kind :other, :note "Ribbuy inference from the word בדיו to include the rings/houses as part of the staves"}], :frame {:text "The Torah uses different terminology for the staves of the various Tabernacle vessels: concerning the ark it writes 'its staves' (Numbers 4:6, Exodus 25:14–15), and concerning the bronze altar similarly (Exodus 27:6–7), whereas concerning the table it writes 'for the houses, for the staves' (Exodus 25:26–27) and concerning the golden altar similarly (Exodus 30:4–5). The phrase 'its staves' is then read expansively to include 'the houses'—the rings that hold the staves.", :sources ["Exodus 25:14–15" "Exodus 25:26–27" "Exodus 27:6–7" "Exodus 30:4–5" "Numbers 4:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic comparison: בדיו used for ark and bronze altar; לבתים לבדים for table and golden altar", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Ribbuy inference from the word בדיו to include the rings/houses as part of the staves", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:23.887901266Z", :model "glm-5.2"}